jobs.description:
SamenvattingStart as an Order Picker in Nieuwegein and make sure Albert Heijn supermarkets receive their products on time. Earn €14.99 gross per hour and allowances for working in shifts. Stay active throughout your working day, work with a friendly team, and make a difference every day. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker at this logistics organization in Nieuwegein, you make sure supermarkets receive their fresh products every day. Using a modern voice-picking system, available in Dutch, English, Polish, and Ukrainian, you collect orders in the warehouse. You walk a lot, pick products from shelves, and prepare orders for transport. You work quickly and accurately, because the stores depend on you. The job takes place in a refrigerated environment (around 4°C), so it’s important you are comfortable with cooler temperatures. You’ll receive clear instructions through the voice-picking system so you know exactly which products to collect.
Your tasks:
- Collecting products using a voice-picking system;
- Preparing and organizing trolleys for shipment;
- Checking product quantities and quality.

This job is for 40 hours per week. Your shifts will be scheduled as follows:
- Morning shift: 05:00–14:30
- Night shift: 19:30–04:00

Over het bedrijfAt your new workplace in Nieuwegein, you’ll work alongside colleagues from different countries towards one shared goal: making sure supermarkets across the Netherlands receive their fresh products on time. The atmosphere is friendly and welcoming. Colleagues help each other when needed, chat during breaks, and always have time for a joke. Together, you contribute to something that people rely on every day.
Wat wij vragen- You have your own accomodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- You speak Dutch, English, or Polish;
- You’re physically fit and able to perform physical work;
- You’re comfortable working in a chilled environment (around 4°C);
- You’re flexible and willing to work week

As a Warehouse Employee at DHL in Weert, you’ll be responsible for various logistics activities within the warehouse. Your tasks may include receiving, checking, storing, picking, and preparing goods for shipment. You’ll also work with Material Handling Equipment (MHE), such as an EPT or stacker, after receiving the appropriate training.

You’ll make sure that products are processed accurately and efficiently and that the warehouse runs smoothly. Because you’ll be working with ASML-related products, precision, responsibility, and following procedures are very important.

- You are 18 years or older (due to working hours);
- You have previous work experience in logistics, warehousing, or a similar environment;
- You’re available full-time (40 hours per week), either in two shifts or during the day;
- You’re able to request a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You have a basic understanding of English, as it is used daily in the warehouse;
- You’re eager to learn new skills, such as operating an EPT or stacker;
- You are comfortable working in a structured and fast-paced logistics environment.

As a Stock Control Officer, you are the guardian of our inventory and therefore a crucial link in the entire logistics process. Without you, everything comes to a standstill. 

De taken:

- Checking, analyzing, and correcting inventory discrepancies;
- Performing cycle counts and inventories;
- Identifying deviations and opportunities for improvement;
- Collaborating with warehouse staff and team leaders;
- Ensuring accurate administration in the system;
- You ensure that colleagues can rely on the correct quantities at the right time.

- You work accurately and have a strong sense of responsibility;
- You are stress-resistant and think in solutions;
- You speak and understand good English;
- You’re able to request a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You are 18 years or older (due to working hours);
- You are willing to work in 2 shifts: 6:00 AM - 3:00 PM / 3:00 PM - 12:00 AM;
- You have an affinity for logistics and inventory management;
- Preferably experience with EPT, reach truck, or OPT
- Additionally, you have good knowledge of Microsoft Office, especially Microsoft Excel.
